  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch17-16> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch17-16--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch17-16--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch17-16: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.86" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.861"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.88"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The taxa, direction and approximate logarithmic relation are quantitatively testable with abundant scans. Standard registration and competing-model evaluation can resolve the geometric claim, though not its developmental interpretation." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Register dense landmarks on human, chimpanzee and baboon skulls, fit one continuous deformation with log-linear area expansion along the stated axes, and compare held-out error with modular craniofacial models." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Age, sex and allometry require control.", "A good integral mapping does not prove a single developmental process." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch17-16--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch17-16--gpt--dataset-2> .
